on't  work point two says that general social  distancing is unlikely or it's unclear  whether that will be effective so  they're not really sure about that point  three and this brings us up to the  present day  they say that they agree that for  example school  closures and household isolation could  be effective when it's kept in place for  a long period and now we come to point  four and this is where what I think is  really important here they say that  these measures to be effective would  need to be in place for at least most of  a year quote under such a policy at  least half of the year will be spent  under the stricter social distancing  measures in other words there'll be a  bit of alternation half the year we'd be  a that would be able to to have kind of  less strict social distancing half the  year very strict this is possibly even  more strict than we are currently seeing  with school closures and everything  that's a year that is considerably  longer than twelve weeks that we are  going to be responding to this and again  I should stress when what the Prime  Minister was talking about he was  talking about flattening the curve or  kind of damping down the sombrero as he  likes to put it he was talking about the  Medical Response this is the behavioral  and social interventions but reading  this it brings home exactly what this is  going to mean for all of us
 

